.TH WMTHEME 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmtheme \- show how the wm-desktop tools see your Window Maker theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmtheme
show | path
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBshow\fR prints the menu colours, textures (kind and every colour) and fonts that wmnotify and wmfiles use, and
how many defaults files they came from: your WindowMaker defaults file, then the global one, then Window Maker's
built-in values. \fBpath\fR prints the user defaults file that is watched for theme changes
($WMAKER_USER_ROOT/Defaults/WindowMaker, default ~/GNUstep/Defaults/WindowMaker).
Run it first when something does not look like your theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify (1),
.BR wmfiles (1)
